  "articleBody": "It's great to tackle home projects, but there are definitely times when bringing in an expert for log cabin trim repair is the smartest move. Here are some key signals that it's time to call a professional:\n\n*   **Extensive rot:** If the trim rot has spread into the adjoining logs, that's a complex fix that needs professional expertise.\n*   **Profile matching challenges:** If the repair requires matching a specific, intricate trim profile, or if you need scarfing (a specialized woodworking joint) to blend new wood seamlessly, a pro can ensure a perfect match.\n*   **Structural or highly visible trim:** For trim that's critical to the cabin's structure or is in a very prominent spot, you want the repair to be done right and look flawless.\n*   **Unknown finish systems:** If you're not sure what kind of stain or finish is on your trim, a professional can test it to ensure any new materials or coatings are compatible.\n*   **Persistent moisture issues:** If you've tried repairs but keep having problems with water intrusion, an expert can diagnose and fix the root cause.\n\nWhile some minor trim issues can be DIY, bringing in someone with experience for these bigger challenges can save you headaches and ensure the longevity and beauty of your log cabin.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
